## 2. Definitions

**"You"** means the person or organization using the Team Software. An organization includes its
affiliates.

**"User"** means a person who has an account in the Team Software's multi-person mode, or who has
used it at any time in the previous thirty (30) days.

**"Subscription"** means a paid ghostfleet Team subscription bought from the Licensor for a stated
number of Users and period.

**"Licensor"** means Pablo Sebastián Garcés Barona, or a company to which he transfers the Team
Software.

## 3. What You may do without paying

You may use, copy and modify the Team Software:
- (a) in production, if You have **no more than two (2) Users**;
- (b) with any number of Users, only to develop, test or evaluate it, and not for any work that
  You would otherwise do for real.

## 4. What needs a Subscription

You need a Subscription covering every User to use the Team Software in production with **three
(3) or more Users**.

Using it beyond the Users or period of Your Subscription needs a larger Subscription.

## 5. What You may not do

You may not:
- (a) provide the Team Software, or a modified version, to third parties as a hosted or managed
